# spin24star STOCK MARKET bot: the paired-hedge commands (/pair, /pairs,
# /delpair, /run, /stoprun, /runs, /runlog) driving Evolution's "Stock Market
# Live" on spin24star.com -- acc1 bets UP, acc2 bets DOWN on the same round,
# both positions cashed out together, so money mostly moves between the two
# accounts. No signup commands (those live on .env.spin24star).
#
# WHAT IS VERIFIED LIVE (2026-11-22), so nobody re-derives it:
#   * login()          -- the bot's own login on real accounts: header LOGIN
#                         (button.rj__login) -> #login_khelo_* form, confirmed
#                         through the site's own GET /api/getBalance.
#   * the table route  -- like winclash, no lobby tile: the engine opens the
#                         site's own /casinoRedirect launch URL with Stock
#                         Market's id (1584, from spin24star's own catalogue).
#                         It lands on ezugi.evo-games.com, table_id
#                         StockMarket00001 -- the same table every other site
#                         here reaches.
#   * the read path    -- verify_stockmarket.py PASSED twice: live table in
#                         83-93s, UP/DOWN bet spots and cash-out present,
#                         3 windows in 60s / 5 in 90s.
#
# WHAT IS *NOT* VERIFIED, and it matters before any real run:
#   * NO BET HAS EVER BEEN PLACED ON THIS SITE. Every test account held 0.00,
#     so placing, settling, cash-out and the hedge are untested here. With a
#     0.00 balance the in-game balance read came back empty, so check that a
#     funded account's balance reads before trusting the run summary.
#   * Accounts carrying BONUS money: the site's own tile handler asks
#     "real or bonus chips?" when there is a bonus balance. The engine opens
#     the launch URL without that choice; which wallet the table then uses
#     has not been seen.
#
# So: fund two accounts, run
#     .venv/bin/python verify_stockmarket.py <user> <pass> --url https://spin24star.com/
# then a single "/run <pair> 10 1" (table minimum is 10 rupees) and read
# /runlog before scaling either the amount or the rounds.
TELEGRAM_BOT_TOKEN=your-spin24star-stockmarket-bot-token-from-botfather
# One id, or several comma-/space-separated ids for multiple master admins:
# MASTER_ADMIN_ID=111111111,222222222
MASTER_ADMIN_ID=your-telegram-user-id

# REQUIRED here, unlike cricmatch/khelofun. spin24star's AWS WAF starts
# answering page loads with a hard captcha after a few automated logins from
# one IP (measured 2026-11-22); each seat's login then pays one solve.
# Without a key a run fails with a clear message rather than hanging.
CAPSOLVER_API_KEY=your-capsolver-api-key

BOT_MODE=stockmarket
BOT_SITE_URL=https://spin24star.com/
ADMINS_FILE=admins.spin24star.stockmarket.json
SETTINGS_FILE=bot_settings.spin24star.stockmarket.json
ADMIN_PHONES_FILE=admin_phones.spin24star.stockmarket.json
# Pair credentials + run history. MUST be distinct from every other
# instance's files -- each process reads them once at import and rewrites
# them whole on every save, so two bots sharing a path silently clobber
# each other. (pairs.* holds plaintext passwords; both patterns are
# gitignored.)
PAIRS_FILE=pairs.spin24star.stockmarket.json
PAIR_RUNS_FILE=pair_runs.spin24star.stockmarket.json

# How many /run hedge sessions may execute at once (each drives two Chromium
# browsers). Default 3.
# MAX_CONCURRENT_RUNS=3

# Proxy: set it from Telegram with /setproxy once the bot is up. Use a FIXED
# residential IP, never the rotating mobile gateway the signup bot runs on --
# a solved WAF token is bound to the exit IP it was minted from, and a
# per-connection rotating proxy changes that IP before the token is used.
